Engine: the galaxy map fleet box's scroll row, "FBSC" (open fix 59).

STATUS: APPLIED 30 September 2026 by work order 194 (Part B; reserved by
work order 193) — orion2re 6f87c151 on orionlayer-local (before: 750434ef), this
file's diff byte for byte (index lines included). Required by
tools/version_check.py since work order 194.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_fleet_box_scroll.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert 6f87c151` or `patch -R -p1`,
and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    FLEETPOP builds the fleet box's ship cells from _fltpop_scroll_bar's
    first_visible_row (fleetpop.cpp:643-644: the first cell is the row
    times 3) and resets it when a stack opens (Initialize_Scroll_Bar_,
    fleetpop.cpp:1324-1332); SerializeState sent only MOX::_scroll_bar, a
    different bar. So a client could not say which three rows of a stack
    past nine ships the box shows — work order 191's item 1, carried into
    193's list. Block "FBSC", after CTGT, only on SCREEN_MAIN while
    moveable box 2 shows a stack (FSEL's own condition): version, the
    stack, first_visible_row, visible_rows, total_rows, and the field ids
    of the bar's up and down buttons.

    Only reads. An engine without OrionLayer behaves exactly as before. One
    marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 59.`, on the block's first comment
    lines.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 7ea40161..a57bae95 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1616,6 +1616,33 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
                 src, MOX::_missile[m].x, MOX::_missile[m].y))));
         }
     }
+
+    // 23. The galaxy map fleet box's scroll row: "FBSC", written ONLY while
+    //     the fleet box (moveable box 2) shows a stack, after CTGT (work
+    //     order 191's item 1). OrionLayer, open fix 59.
+    //
+    //     FLEETPOP builds its ship cells from _fltpop_scroll_bar's
+    //     first_visible_row (fleetpop.cpp: _first_fleet_movement_icon = row
+    //     * 3) and resets it when a new stack opens (Initialize_Scroll_Bar_);
+    //     SerializeState sent only MOX::_scroll_bar, a different bar. So a
+    //     client could not say which three rows of a stack past nine ships
+    //     the box shows. The row, the bar's rows, and its two buttons' fields.
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_MAIN && MOVEBOX::Moveable_Box_Selected_(2) &&
+        MOX::_fleet_box_ship_stack >= 0 &&
+        MOX::_fleet_box_ship_stack < MOX::_ship_stack_count) {
+        const s_scroll_bar& bar = MOX::_fltpop_scroll_bar;
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'F');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'B');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'S');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'C');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_box_ship_stack);
+        Write16(buf, bar.first_visible_row);
+        Write16(buf, bar.visible_rows);
+        Write16(buf, bar.total_rows);
+        Write16(buf, bar.up_btn);
+        Write16(buf, bar.dn_btn);
+    }
 }
 
